{
  "_README": [
    "What each steading improvement REQUIRES, and what it DOES. Hand-authored and reviewed against",
    "Book I/II; merged onto the pack items by scripts/import/build-improvement-effects.js.",
    "",
    "Kept outside packs/src/ so regenerating steading-improvements/additional/ cannot destroy it.",
    "",
    "`requires` is an expression over the improvement's own row slugs:",
    "  \"slug\"                    that row, ticked through",
    "  { all: [ ... ] }          every term",
    "  { any: 2, of: [ ... ] }   at least two of them (any without a number means one)",
    "",
    "`when.kind` is completed | turn (with seasons; empty = every season) | moment.",
    "There is no `lapsed`: 'if you cease to meet the requirements, decrease Prosperity by 1' is the",
    "same result's requirement going false again.",
    "",
    "A result is APPLIED by the sheet only when it carries a plain integer `change` or a `listEntry`",
    "and has no `condition` and no `adjustment`. Everything else is stated and left to the table.",
    "",
    "Results are addressed as `<slug>:<index into this list>` by the sheet's per-line opt-outs, so",
    "REORDERING an improvement's effects moves those ticks. Harmless in practice — opt-outs are",
    "season-scoped and cleared when the wheel turns — but append rather than insert where you can."
  ],
  "additional-housing": {
    "requires": {
      "all": [
        {
          "any": 1,
          "of": [
            "engineer-foreman",
            "build-on-fields"
          ]
        },
        "pull-together"
      ]
    },
    "effects": [
      {
        "when": {
          "kind": "completed"
        },
        "change": {
          "target": "fortunes",
          "amount": 1
        },
        "text": "increase Fortunes by 1"
      },
      {
        "when": {
          "kind": "completed"
        },
        "text": "add any new homes to the map"
      },
      {
        "when": {
          "kind": "turn",
          "seasons": [
            "winter"
          ]
